------------------------------------------------------------------------
What is your assessment of the assignment? Was it helpful? Was it fun?

It was a pretty straight forward assignment. The replace.c was a little confusing to start, but it started to make sense after I wrote down the different conditions and thought about how to get my memory address to update through each iteration of each char. It definitely took a bit to get the hang of pointers though. The critTer and splint commands were useful to catch the stylistic errors in my code, specifically on finding times when I didn't use the return value of a function (so I had to cast to void according to the error)

